<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms governing Websetly's website performance, technical SEO, optimisation and website development services."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="August 19, 2025"
  path="/terms"
>
  <h2>Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By accessing and using Websetly's services, you accept and agree to be bound
    by the terms and provision of this agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Services</h2>
  <p>
    Websetly provides website performance and growth services including but not
    limited to performance optimisation, Core Web Vitals remediation, technical
    SEO, accessibility auditing, conversion optimisation, website monitoring and
    maintenance, together with website design and development, hosting assistance
    and digital consultation.
  </p>

  <h2>Reports and measurements</h2>
  <p>
    Reports produced by our website analyzer are generated from third-party data,
    including the Google PageSpeed Insights API and the Chrome User Experience
    Report. They are provided for information only. Measurements vary between
    runs, devices and networks, and a report does not constitute a guarantee of
    any particular ranking, score or commercial outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Client responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide accurate and complete information required for project completion</li>
    <li>Respond to requests for feedback and approval in a timely manner</li>
    <li>Make payments according to the agreed schedule</li>
    <li>Respect intellectual property rights</li>
    <li>
      Provide the access required to carry out agreed work, including to hosting,
      source control and analytics where relevant
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment terms</h2>
  <p>
    Payment terms will be specified in individual project agreements. Generally,
    we require a 50% deposit before work begins, with the remainder due upon
    project completion.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Upon full payment, clients will own the rights to their custom website design
    and content. Websetly retains the right to showcase completed work in our
    portfolio.
  </p>

  <h2>Revisions and changes</h2>
  <p>
    Each project includes a specified number of revision rounds. Additional
    revisions beyond the agreed scope may incur additional charges.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    Websetly's liability shall not exceed the total amount paid for services. We
    are not responsible for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages.
  </p>

  <h2>Termination</h2>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate the agreement with written notice. Upon
    termination, payment is due for all work completed to date.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
